citations.translation:
The tenant may sublet the property in whole or in part with the landlord's consent.

The landlord may only refuse consent if:
a. the tenant refuses to inform the landlord of the terms of the sublet;
b. the terms of the sublet are abusive compared to those of the main lease;
c. substantial disadvantages would arise for the landlord from the sublet.

The tenant is liable to the landlord for ensuring the subtenant does not use the property differently than the tenant is permitted to.

